* Recursive factorial via DEFINE/RETURN. This exercises the
* save/restore call-frame discipline for real: N is a single global
* variable, but each recursive FACT(N-1) call saves the caller's N,
* binds its own, and restores the caller's N on return -- so recursion
* works correctly even though nothing here is lexically scoped.
        DEFINE('FACT(N)')
        OUTPUT = FACT(5)
END     N = N
FACT    LE(N,1)                  :S(BASE)
        FACT = N * FACT(N - 1)   :(RETURN)
BASE    FACT = 1                 :(RETURN)
